.TH "PERCH-MAIL-SEND" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-mail\-send \- compose and send a message
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch mail send [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Compose a MIME message and submit it through SMTP. Text and HTML bodies are combined as multipart/alternative; attachments wrap the result in multipart/mixed.
.PP
Bodies come from \-\-body/\-\-body\-file and \-\-html\-body/\-\-html\-file, or stdin when it is not a terminal. Attachments are base64 encoded and content types are detected from the file extension or contents.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Bodies are quoted\-printable unless \-\-8bitmime is set; attachments are base64.
.IP \(bu 2
SMTPUTF8 is detected from non\-ASCII envelope addresses and extra headers; force it with \-\-smtputf8.
.IP \(bu 2
Bcc recipients are envelope\-only and never appear in headers.
.IP \(bu 2
SIZE is sent automatically and checked against the server's advertised limit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-username, \-u <value>
account username (env PERCH_IMAP_USER)
.TP
.B \-\-password <value>
account password (prefer PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD or \-\-password\-file)
.TP
.B \-\-password\-file <value>
read the account password from a file
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
read the account password from stdin
.TP
.B \-\-timeout <value>
connection timeout (default: 30s)
.TP
.B \-\-config <value>
configuration file (default: ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-from <value>
sender address (default: \-\-username)
.TP
.B \-\-to <value>...
recipient address or list; repeatable
.TP
.B \-\-cc <value>...
Cc recipient address or list; repeatable
.TP
.B \-\-bcc <value>...
Bcc recipient address or list; repeatable
.TP
.B \-\-reply\-to <value>...
Reply\-To address or list; repeatable
.TP
.B \-\-subject, \-s <value>
message subject
.TP
.B \-\-body <value>
plain\-text body
.TP
.B \-\-body\-file <value>
read the plain\-text body from a file (use \- for stdin)
.TP
.B \-\-html\-body <value>
HTML body
.TP
.B \-\-html\-file <value>
read the HTML body from a file (use \- for stdin)
.TP
.B \-\-attach, \-a <value>...
attach a file; repeatable
.TP
.B \-\-header, \-H <value>...
add an extra header (Name: Value); repeatable
.TP
.B \-\-in\-reply\-to <value>
Message\-ID being replied to
.TP
.B \-\-references <value>
space\-separated Message\-IDs for References
.TP
.B \-\-8bitmime
send UTF\-8 text with BODY=8BITMIME
.TP
.B \-\-smtputf8
force SMTPUTF8 (usually detected automatically)
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run, \-n
write the composed message to stdout without sending
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
print SMTP capabilities and delivery details to stderr
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-server, \-S <value>
SMTP submission server (smtps://host, smtp://host, or host[:port]); defaults from \-\-config
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-plaintext
connect to SMTP without TLS (use only on trusted networks)
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-starttls
require STARTTLS for SMTP
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-implicit\-tls
use implicit TLS for SMTP (usually port 465)
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-insecure
skip SMTP TLS certificate verification
.TP
.B \-\-smtp\-ca\-file <value>
PEM CA bundle used to verify the SMTP server certificate
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch mail send \-\-from you@example.com \-\-to alice@example.com \\
  \-\-subject Hello \-\-body 'Hi Alice'

echo 'Body from stdin' | perch mail send \-\-from you@example.com \\
  \-\-to alice@example.com \-\-subject Hello

perch mail send \-\-from you@example.com \-\-to alice@example.com \\
  \-\-subject Report \-\-body\-file message.txt \-\-html\-file message.html \\
  \-\-attach report.pdf

perch mail send ... \-\-dry\-run > message.eml
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_USER
default account username and sender
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD
account password
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1), \fBperch\-mail\fR(1)
